{"content_hash": "d68cc402d5b15c93", "version_id": 554, "article_id": 56, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "title_zh": "加拿大诗人安妮·卡森拿下诺贝尔文学奖", "has_translation": true, "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq4g1j54nepyo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586859411132-573998709aa9?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8Ym9sZCUyMGludmVudGl2ZSUyMGNhbmFkaWFufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NzgxOTd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Isabel Piñeiro on Unsplash", "author": "Isabel Piñeiro", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@isabelpinheiro?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-and-white-flag-on-rock-formation-near-body-of-water-during-daytime-MJFBzRgEqEc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(250, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(288, 46%, 48%)", "label": "CULTURE", "seed": "45e27dcc686b"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 215, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "The Swedish Academy has awarded the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature to Canadian poet Anne Carson. The 76-year-old is known for writing that mixes poetry, fiction and classical scholarship.", "lead_zh": "瑞典学院将2026年诺贝尔文学奖授予加拿大诗人安妮·卡森。这位76岁的作家以融合诗歌、小说和古典学术的写作闻名。", "preview": "Carson was honoured for a \"bold and inventive\" body of work that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms fo", "preview_zh": "卡森获奖的理由是她的作品“大胆而富有创意”，在与古典传统的俏皮对话中为当代文学创造了新形式。诺贝尔奖表彰的是终身写作成就，被视为世界文学界最负盛名的奖项。获奖者将得到1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑或120万美元。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 542, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/56/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 85.062, "size_bytes": 514080, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 249, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/554.json", "paragraphs": ["Carson was honoured for a \"bold and inventive\" body of work that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature. The Nobel is given for a lifetime of writing and is seen as the most prestigious prize in world literature. The winner receives 12 million Swedish kronor, about £900,000 or $1.2m.", "When told the news by phone, Carson joked that the judges were \"crazy\" to choose her. She was staying in Iceland at the time, where she was listening to the wind. Ingrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said Carson was taken by surprise but very happy, and that she could hear it in her voice.", "Born in Toronto in 1950, Carson now lives in Michigan and has held Icelandic citizenship since 2022. She has taught classics for more than 30 years, and her writing is often inspired by Greek literature. Her notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red, Nox and Float.", "Anders Olsson, who chairs the Nobel committee, praised how Carson broke away from lyrical poetry tied to the narrative self and inspired new forms of writing. Her work moves between classical and modern poetry, and between different genres and artforms. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called the win a proud moment for Canada."], "paragraphs_zh": ["卡森获奖的理由是她的作品“大胆而富有创意”，在与古典传统的俏皮对话中为当代文学创造了新形式。诺贝尔奖表彰的是终身写作成就，被视为世界文学界最负盛名的奖项。获奖者将得到1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑或120万美元。", "接到电话通知时，卡森开玩笑说评委选她是“疯了”。她当时正在冰岛，听着风声。瑞典学院常任秘书英格丽德·卡尔贝里说，卡森感到意外，但非常高兴，她从对方的声音里就能听出来。", "卡森1950年生于多伦多，现居密歇根，自2022年起还拥有冰岛国籍。她教授古典学超过30年，写作常受希腊文学启发。她的代表作包括《玻璃随笔》《红色自传》《夜》和《漂浮》。", "诺贝尔委员会主席安德斯·奥尔松称赞卡森摆脱了依附于叙事自我的抒情诗，激发了新的写作形式。她的作品游走于古典与现代诗歌之间，也跨越不同体裁和艺术形式。加拿大总理马克·卡尼称这次获奖是加拿大的骄傲时刻。"], "body": "Carson was honoured for a \"bold and inventive\" body of work that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature. The Nobel is given for a lifetime of writing and is seen as the most prestigious prize in world literature. The winner receives 12 million Swedish kronor, about £900,000 or $1.2m.\n\nWhen told the news by phone, Carson joked that the judges were \"crazy\" to choose her. She was staying in Iceland at the time, where she was listening to the wind. Ingrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said Carson was taken by surprise but very happy, and that she could hear it in her voice.\n\nBorn in Toronto in 1950, Carson now lives in Michigan and has held Icelandic citizenship since 2022. She has taught classics for more than 30 years, and her writing is often inspired by Greek literature. Her notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red, Nox and Float.\n\nAnders Olsson, who chairs the Nobel committee, praised how Carson broke away from lyrical poetry tied to the narrative self and inspired new forms of writing. Her work moves between classical and modern poetry, and between different genres and artforms. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called the win a proud moment for Canada.", "body_zh": "卡森获奖的理由是她的作品“大胆而富有创意”，在与古典传统的俏皮对话中为当代文学创造了新形式。诺贝尔奖表彰的是终身写作成就，被视为世界文学界最负盛名的奖项。获奖者将得到1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑或120万美元。\n\n接到电话通知时，卡森开玩笑说评委选她是“疯了”。她当时正在冰岛，听着风声。瑞典学院常任秘书英格丽德·卡尔贝里说，卡森感到意外，但非常高兴，她从对方的声音里就能听出来。\n\n卡森1950年生于多伦多，现居密歇根，自2022年起还拥有冰岛国籍。她教授古典学超过30年，写作常受希腊文学启发。她的代表作包括《玻璃随笔》《红色自传》《夜》和《漂浮》。\n\n诺贝尔委员会主席安德斯·奥尔松称赞卡森摆脱了依附于叙事自我的抒情诗，激发了新的写作形式。她的作品游走于古典与现代诗歌之间，也跨越不同体裁和艺术形式。加拿大总理马克·卡尼称这次获奖是加拿大的骄傲时刻。", "text": "Carson was honoured for a \"bold and inventive\" body of work that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature. The Nobel is given for a lifetime of writing and is seen as the most prestigious prize in world literature. The winner receives 12 million Swedish kronor, about £900,000 or $1.2m. When told the news by phone, Carson joked that the judges were \"crazy\" to choose her. She was staying in Iceland at the time, where she was listening to the wind. Ingrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said Carson was taken by surprise but very happy, and that she could hear it in her voice. Born in Toronto in 1950, Carson now lives in Michigan and has held Icelandic citizenship since 2022. She has taught classics for more than 30 years, and her writing is often inspired by Greek literature. Her notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red, Nox and Float. Anders Olsson, who chairs the Nobel committee, praised how Carson broke away from lyrical poetry tied to the narrative self and inspired new forms of writing. Her work moves between classical and modern poetry, and between different genres and artforms. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called the win a proud moment for Canada.", "vocab": [{"word": "prestigious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有声望的，享有盛誉的", "note": "常与 award, prize, university 搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "award", "pos": "verb", "zh": "授予，颁发", "note": "常用被动：be awarded the prize", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "honour", "pos": "verb", "zh": "表彰，授予荣誉", "note": "英式拼写，美式为 honor", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inventive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有创意的，善于创新的", "note": "形容人或作品富有新意", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "oeuvre", "pos": "noun", "zh": "（某作家的）全部作品", "note": "来自法语，文学评论常用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "contemporary", "pos": "adj", "zh": "当代的，现代的", "note": "contemporary literature 当代文学", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "genre", "pos": "noun", "zh": "体裁，类型", "note": "如小说、诗歌、戏剧等", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "take by surprise", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "使吃惊，出乎意料", "note": "常用被动：be taken by surprise", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "scholarship", "pos": "noun", "zh": "学术研究，学问", "note": "此处指学术性写作，不是奖学金", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "translation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "翻译，译本", "note": "动词为 translate", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "classics", "pos": "noun", "zh": "古典学，古典文学", "note": "指古希腊罗马文学研究", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "break away from", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "摆脱，脱离", "note": "后接传统、习惯等", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "summary_original": "Carson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.", "body_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize\nBy\nIan Youngs\nCulture reporter\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nCanadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson has been awarded this year's Nobel Prize in Literature.\nCarson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross the boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.\nThe Nobel Prize committee said they had selected her \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\".\nCarson responded by joking that the judges were \"crazy\" for honouring her. \"I think they're all crazy... Well, you know, it's crazy,\" she told public broadcaster RUV in Iceland, where she is currently staying.\nThe Nobel Prize is awarded for a lifetime's body of work and is regarded as the most prestigious award in global literature, with the winner receiving 12 million Swedish kronor (£900,000, $1.2m).\nIngrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said she had broken the news to Carson on the phone shortly before the public announcement.\n\"She had time to tell me was that she is, for the moment, in Iceland, where she is listening to the wind,\" Carlberg, said.\n\"She was taken by surprise but very happy. I could hear that in her voice.\"\nBorn in Toronto in 1950, Carson lives in Michigan and has also held Icelandic citizenship since 2022.\nAnders Olsson, chairman of the Swedish Academy's Nobel committee for Literature, praised the way Carson has \"broken away from lyrical poetry bound to the narrative self and inspired new forms of contemporary literature\".\n\"This method of writing leads to playful and ironic works that move not only between classical and modern poetry but also between different genres and artforms,\" he said.\nCanadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Carson's win was \"an extraordinary achievement and a proud moment for Canada\".\nThe writer's works feature \"wit, imagination, and a style entirely her own,\" Carney wrote on social media.\n\"She has brought ancient stories to new audiences and transformed the way we think about literature.\"\n'Outstanding importance'\nCarson's notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red: A Novel in Verse, Nox, Float and The Beauty of the Husband: A Fictional Essay in 29 Tangos.\nIn 2019, her performance piece Norma Jeane Baker of Troy drew a line between famous beauties from different historical periouds - Helen of Troy and Marilyn Monroe.\nIn 2021, she released The Trojan Women: A Comic, a graphic retelling of Euripides' ancient story; and her translation of Elektra by Sophocles was staged starring Brie Larson in London last year.\nShe has been a professor of classics for more than 30 years and her writing is often inspired by Greek literature.\nHer translations have often given a contemporary twist to ancient works.\n\"Her collaborations with visual artists and choreographers and with opera and theatre directors demonstrate the freedom with which she relates to literary expectations and rule systems,\" Olsson said.\n\"It is this that lies behind the outstanding importance her work since the 1990s has had for the international art and literature scene.\"\nRelated topics\nBooks\nLiterature\nNobel Prize\nMore on this story\nHungarian author László Krasznahorkai wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n9 October 2025\nSouth Korea's Han Kang wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n10 October 2024\nNorway's Jon Fosse wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n5 October 2023", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:23:16.183990", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Carson", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.562, "sm": 100, "em": 562, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "was", "s": 0.575, "e": 0.712, "sm": 575, "em": 712, "cs": 7, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "honoured", "s": 0.725, "e": 1.113, "sm": 725, "em": 1112, "cs": 11, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "for", "s": 1.125, "e": 1.312, "sm": 1125, "em": 1312, "cs": 20, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "a", "s": 1.325, "e": 1.387, "sm": 1325, "em": 1387, "cs": 24, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "\"", "s": 1.387, "e": 1.438, "sm": 1387, "em": 1437, "cs": 26, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "bold", "s": 1.438, "e": 1.762, "sm": 1437, "em": 1762, "cs": 27, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "and", "s": 1.775, "e": 1.875, "sm": 1775, "em": 1875, "cs": 32, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "inventive", "s": 1.887, "e": 2.4, "sm": 1887, "em": 2400, "cs": 36, "ce": 45, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "\"", "s": 2.4, "e": 2.45, "sm": 2400, "em": 2450, "cs": 45, "ce": 46, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "body", "s": 2.45, "e": 2.75, "sm": 2450, "em": 2750, "cs": 47, "ce": 51, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "of", "s": 2.763, "e": 2.85, "sm": 2762, "em": 2850, "cs": 52, "ce": 54, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "work", "s": 2.862, "e": 3.162, "sm": 2862, "em": 3162, "cs": 55, "ce": 59, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "that", "s": 3.175, "e": 3.438, "sm": 3175, "em": 3437, "cs": 60, "ce": 64, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": ",", "s": 3.438, "e": 3.562, "sm": 3437, "em": 3562, "cs": 64, "ce": 65, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "in", "s": 3.562, "e": 3.712, "sm": 3562, "em": 3712, "cs": 66, "ce": 68, "si": 0}, {"i": 16, "w": "playful", "s": 3.725, "e": 4.138, "sm": 3725, "em": 4137, "cs": 69, "ce": 76, "si": 0}, {"i": 17, "w": "dialogue", "s": 4.15, "e": 4.7, "sm": 4150, "em": 4700, "cs": 77, "ce": 85, "si": 0}, {"i": 18, "w": "with", "s": 4.713, "e": 4.825, "sm": 4712, "em": 4825, "cs": 86, "ce": 90, "si": 0}, 